@startuml fdcache
'
' Engineered by  Christian Schnapka
'                Embedded Principal+ Engineer
'                Macstab GmbH · Hamburg, Germany
'                https://macstab.com
'
' libchaos-io process-wide fd cache: direct-mapped lookup with a per-slot
' seqlock and generation, /proc/self/fd miss resolution, and every
' invalidation trigger.
'
' Reference: docs/IO.md §6 "FD cache", docs/ARCHITECTURE.md "FD Path Resolution"
'            src/config/chaos_io_fdcache.c, src/wrappers/chaos_io_sync.c
'
title libchaos-io Process-Wide FD Cache — Lookup and Invalidation

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 4
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor                 #2C3E50
  LifeLineBorderColor        #2C3E50
  LifeLineBackgroundColor    #ECF0F1
  ParticipantBorderColor     #2C3E50
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantFontStyle       bold
  GroupBackgroundColor       #FDFEFE
  GroupBorderColor           #95A5A6
}
hide footbox

participant "Wrapper\n(read/write/fsync/…)" as Wrap
participant "FD Cache\n(process-wide, 32 slots)" as Cache
participant "/proc/self/fd\n<fd>" as Proc
participant "Config Engine" as Config
participant "Real function" as Real

note over Cache
  Table: 32 × {sequence, generation, fd + 1, PATH_MAX path},
  mapped on the first store with raw SYS_mmap (no allocator,
  not visible to libchaos-memory); a concurrent mapper that
  loses the CAS unmaps. Mapping failed: every lookup misses.
  Generations: static array outside the table, so an
  invalidation never needs the mapping.
end note

== Descriptor-based call (fd > 2, after prepare() found rules) ==

Wrap -> Cache : lookup(fd)
note right of Cache
  slot = fd % 32
  hit only if: sequence even and unchanged across the copy,
  slot holds fd, entry generation == slot generation
end note

alt Cache hit
  Cache --> Wrap : path
else Cache miss
  Wrap -> Cache : generation = slot generation (read first)
  Wrap -> Proc : readlink("/proc/self/fd/<fd>")\n(under the guard, errno restored)
  note right of Proc
    Kernel name, links resolved
    (pipe:[N], socket:[N], anon_inode:[...] for non-files).
    Excluded: /proc, /sys, /dev, /tmp/.chaos-*:
    no match, not cached.
  end note
  Proc --> Wrap : path
  Wrap -> Cache : store_at(fd, path, generation)
  note right of Cache
    seqlock CAS even → odd; skipped if the slot is
    busy. The entry keeps the generation read before
    readlink: if a close bumped it meanwhile, the
    entry is dead on arrival and never returned.
  end note
end

Wrap -> Config : select one rule (operation, path)
Config --> Wrap : rule or none
Wrap -> Real : real_function(fd, …)
Real --> Wrap : result

== open-style call returns a descriptor ==

note over Wrap, Cache
  fd = real_open(...) for open, openat, creat, fopen, freopen:
  1. invalidate(fd): drop what an fd closed behind io's back left
  2. resolve(fd): cache the kernel's name, links resolved
end note

== Invalidation: atomic ++generation[fd % 32], no lock, no waiting ==

note over Wrap, Cache
  • close(fd): after the real close, whatever it returned
    (Linux releases the descriptor even on error)
  • dup2, dup3: newfd, on success (dup2 only if oldfd != newfd)
  • close_range: each fd of the range, on success; a range of 32 or
    more fds resets every slot; CLOSE_RANGE_CLOEXEC invalidates nothing
  • closedir, pclose, fclose: the stream's fd, after the real call
  • freopen: the stream's fd when an injected open fault fires
end note

== Full reset: ++generation of all 32 slots ==

note over Wrap, Cache
  • closefrom(): always
  • unlinkat, renameat, renameat2 and the path forms (unlink, rmdir,
    remove, rename): on success, since any cached path may now name
    another inode
  • library constructor: once
end note

note across
  One table for all threads. An entry is valid only while its slot's
  generation is unchanged, so a close on thread A is seen by thread B
  at once, and a lookup that raced with the close never returns the
  stale path.
end note

@enduml
